!
!  The data in this file are computed from differential scattering 
!  cross section data provided by the Controlled Fusion Atomic Data
!  Center (http://www-cfadc.phy.ornl.gov). Those data and their integrals
!  can be found on that Web site and in P.S. Krstic and D. R. Schultz,
!  Atomic and Plasma-Material Interaction Data for Fusion (Supplement
!  to the journal Nuclear Fusion) 8 (1998).
!
!  The D+ + D data should be equivalent to those found on their Web
!  site with no significant differences  (also, the data shown here extend 
!  down to center-of-mass energies of 1.e-3 eV). The D+ + D2 data were
!  from an earlier calculation and will only qualitatively match the
!  data provided on the Web. These data will be updated as soon as possible.
!
!  The treatment of elastic scattering in a Monte Carlo neutral transport
!  code can be made more efficient by replacing scatterings with deviations
!  smaller than some minimum cutoff angle by an effective scattering at
!  that minimum angle. The total cross section is computed so as to keep
!  the diffusion cross section at its expected value (the viscosity cross
!  section is modified only very slightly). So, data are included here
!  for both no cutoff (for comparison purposes) and a cutoff of 5 degrees.
!
!  A separate set of data provides the scattering angles broken up into
!  bins of equal probability. These data are also used in the Monte Carlo
!  calculation.
!
$ ELS D [+0] (G) D [+1] (G) D [+0] (G) D [+1] (G)
& XST CUTOFF_00 #ELCROSS 
!
!  This is a multi-piece fit to the total elastic scattering cross 
!  section with no cutoff.
!
